.TH FORGEKIT-INSPECT 1 "2026-08-25" "ForgeKit 0.3.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
forgekit-inspect \- Inspect the ForgeKit project signature
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forgekit inspect
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect a ForgeKit project's signature and metadata. Displays project
information, installed features, schema version, and validation status.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIformat\fR
Output format: human, json (default: human)
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Reduce output (except errors and JSON)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Inspect current project:
.B forgekit inspect
.TP
Inspect with JSON output:
.B forgekit inspect --format json
.SH INFORMATION DISPLAYED
.TP
.B Project Name
Name from forge.yaml
.TP
.B Project Type
ForgeKit, legacy, external compatible, or invalid
.TP
.B Schema Version
ForgeKit schema version
.TP
.B Installed Features
List of features with versions and timestamps
.TP
.B Signature Status
Valid, legacy, absent, or invalid
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Project not found or not a ForgeKit project
.TP
.B 2
Execution error
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./forge.yaml
Project metadata
.TP
.I ./.forge/features.yaml
Installed features with versions
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forgekit (1),
.BR forgekit-doctor (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ForgeKit Contributors <forgekit@demetrius-ch.github.io>